Rule 1 (tensor-tensor operands must have identical shapes to compare elementwise)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ if ndim(v_1) = 0 then true else ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i)
>>
Rule 5 (with tensor other, out tensor must match input/other shapes)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ndim(v_3) = ndim(v_1) ∧ if ndim(v_1) = 0 then true else ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i) ∧ shape(v_3, i) = shape(v_1, i)
